  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1213 PM MDT Sat Apr 18 2026\n\nWidespread hard freeze conditions developed overnight in the\nwake of yesterday's cold front and new snowfall. Temperatures\nhave pushed back above freezing late this morning as we head for\na cooler than normal day. The cold front that moved through here\nyesterday continues to plummet towards the Gulf Coast of Texas\nwhich is quite impressive...and will have consequences for us\nearly next week. Another cold night is in store before warmer\nair starts to filter in later on Sunday. Freeze Warnings are in\neffect in a majority of the same areas as last night with the\nexception of the lower desert valleys. There could still be\npockets near to below freezing temperatures in the \nmicro-climate across these zones so stay vigilant if plants or\nplumbing needs to be protected. The bigger picture shows \nridging over the West stuck between anomalous troughs over the \nMidWest and E.Pacific. The ridge will dominate our weather \nthrough early next week as the upstream closed low lingers off \nthe West Coast. This means a return to a warmer temperature\nregime through midweek. Most areas remain dry but the\naformentioned cold front/Plains high pressure strong enough \nthat it will push a plume of return moisture northward into the\n4 Corners region late tomorrow. This mositure lingers over the \narea Monday and Tuesday and looks to bring isolated to widely \nscattered afternoon mountain showers and thunderstorms as the \nheating promotes convection. Wednesday will be the transition \nday as which means wind this time of year and if trends continue\nwind gusts could be impactful. The upstream low marches across \nthe Intermountain West to the Northern Plains to end out the \nweek and usher in a cooler and wetter weather pattern. \nTemperatures look to settle back closer to or slightly below \nnormal with more high elevation snow for the northern and \ncentral mountains Thursday into Friday. Impacts for this late \nweek event look to be more below freezing temperatures for the \nhigher valleys and temporary winter driving conditions over some\nof the passes.",
